 "reports_individuals_with_tnfaip3_variant": true,
 "relevance_note": "Single case report of a woman with a homozygous LCAT variant: 'she had the same mutations in LCAT gene homozygously (c. 440 C>T, p.T147I)' and 'She was diagnosed with fish-eye disease'.",
 "method_note": "Hand-built from a one-paragraph case report; JSON assembled by a short script in scratch, values from my reading. Label 'patient' (rule 5). 'as reported (1)' refers to the mutation having been reported before (ref 1, Funke 1993), not to this patient, so cites_prior_report_of_same_patients is left null. Age 46 is the age at presentation; onset, diagnosis and last-evaluation ages are not stated (last evaluation was after 15 years of observation, age not given), so all left not reported. HDL-C 2 mg/dL is not called 'low' for this patient in the text (only the general statement that FED patients show markedly low HDL-C); recorded observed from the value. LDL-C 105 mg/dL not qualified by the authors: no row, checklist not reported. 'Her complete blood count and renal function were normal' recorded under D-27 as anemia excluded and abnormal renal function excluded; checklist 'chronic kidney disease or renal failure' left not reported because normal renal function is narrower than the composite item. Serum LCAT activity treated as a patient biochemical phenotype, not as a functional assay of the variant. 'no systemic complaints' and best-corrected visual acuity 1.5 not recorded as features (too vague / not qualified). The cardiovascular-disease sentence is general, not about this patient. No contradictions found.",
